2026-11-06T03:17:35.9125310Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9132916Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9133952Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9134756Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9135117Z 
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9135441Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9135892Z 
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9136230Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9137052Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9137355Z 
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9137493Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9137958Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9138212Z 
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9138476Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9138955Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:17:35.9139157Z 
